WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.038
The check reads the register's shape.

2
00:00:02.038 --> 00:00:06.825
The first rule flags a row without a
single writer, or a row listed twice.

3
00:00:06.825 --> 00:00:09.380
Others flag a writer that isn't defined,

4
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:13.213
or one with no identities, so
its writes can't be attributed.

5
00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:17.188
A required account-state transition
with no row is a finding.

6
00:00:17.188 --> 00:00:19.435
So is deletion by inbound provisioning,

7
00:00:19.435 --> 00:00:22.975
since the guide deletes through
the post-separation workflow.

8
00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:25.296
A backstop can't be the writer itself,

9
00:00:25.296 --> 00:00:28.313
and rows for the same
audited change must agree.

10
00:00:28.313 --> 00:00:32.620
An unsigned register and an
unversioned scope filter are warnings.
